-- title:
--   Regularity of the special fibre on the pole chart via purity
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and a natural number $M' \ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and assume some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of that field. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$, and with compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$; let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$. On the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X} =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel` $A\,K\,j$ (the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$), let $z$ be a point, let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}$ obtained from $\varpi$ along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk. Assume $z$ is the image under $\iota_\infty$ of a point $y$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the pole chart $A_\infty(K) =$ `chartAlgInf` $A\,K\,j$ whose prime is maximal and whose prime contains every element of $A_\infty(K)$ that is a non-unit of $W_0$. Let $K_0$ be the corresponding `laurentBaseChange` of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, contained in $K$, with compatible $A$-algebra structure and with a nonzero $j_0 \in K_0$ having the same Laurent expansion $\mathrm{jq}$; let $\iota : A_\infty(K_0) \to A_\infty(K)$ be a ring homomorphism inducing the inclusion $K_0 \subseteq K$ on underlying elements, and assume the structure morphism of the floor model `TwoChartIntegralModel` $A\,K_0\,j_0$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ is smooth. Then, with $A_\infty(K)$ viewed as an $A_\infty(K_0)$-algebra via $\iota$: if $A_\infty(K)$ is unramified over $A_\infty(K_0)$ at every height-one prime $\mathfrak{Q}$ of $A_\infty(K)$ contained in the prime of $y$, then the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the pole-chart form of the purity step in the regularity analysis of the Igusa-level integral model: regularity of the special fibre at a closed point of the $\infty$-branch is deduced from smoothness of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-floor together with unramifiedness in codimension one (Auslander–Buchsbaum freeness for the finite normal cover of a two-dimensional regular local ring, plus purity of the branch locus). It carries no ordinarity or geometric-point data, and feeds the companion result that replaces the codimension-one hypothesis by a localisation criterion at the prime of $y$.
